/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Each satellite has an elevation angle above the horizon and an azimuth angle clockwise from north.
   - Let ui = (ux, uy, uz) be the unit vector from receiver to satellite i.
   - σ_position is the 1-sigma position error in metres; DOP is the chosen dilution factor; σ_range is the 1-sigma range error in metres.
   - Precision is repeatability; accuracy is closeness to true coordinates.
   - A confidence level states the probability contained.
   - Range errors enter every satellite.
   - DOP does not fix any of these.
*/
