/* book exam traps: Treating high elevation as good geometry. DOP depends on how the line-of-sight directions are spread, not on elevation alone, not on signal strength and not on range distance. | Confusing DOP with accuracy. DOP scales random range noise; it does not remove ionosphere, multipath or ephemeris bias. | Saying CEP is 95%. CEP is about 50%; 2DRMS is the usual about-95% horizontal measure. | Forgetting the clock term. GDOP and TDOP include clock; HDOP and VDOP do not. | Assuming more satellites always lower DOP. A new satellite in the same cluster may barely change the geometry. */
